{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1038525-adapting-mage-dark-ages-to-2nd-ed-mage","id":1038525,"title":"Adapting Mage Dark ages to 2nd Ed Mage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-26T12:43:54-08:00","id":1038525,"title":"Adapting Mage Dark ages to 2nd Ed Mage","content":"Has any one done a conversion or adaptation of DA:Mage from oWoD?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust","name":"bestial Warlust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T12:55:39-08:00","id":1038535,"title":"","content":"Dark Ages is Mage 2e already. Unless you're talking about some Dark Ages game not involving the People?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T12:57:16-08:00","id":1038538,"title":"","content":"You mean converting the game over? There's a <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114433/Mage-Translation-Guide?\" target=\"_blank\">Mage Translation Guide</a> for that, but I don't know if it has Dark Ages stuff.<br /> <br /> Or do you mean just using the time, and having Awakening in the Dark Ages? Because in that case there's only To The Strongest so far, which takes place in 330-320 BCE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T13:29:15-08:00","id":1038552,"title":"","content":"Not that I'm aware of... I'm not sure what the point would be. Dark Eras already covers running the CofD games in the past; even if DA wasn't a focus of Mage.<br /> <br /> What would be the goal of this adaptation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T14:27:58-08:00","id":1038579,"title":"","content":"Taking mage to an earlier setting. There probably wouldn't be much change as the orders have been around for a long time. I'll have to take a look at Dark Era's and see what's in there. I wouldn't want to convert mechanics I was thinking more of setting fluff than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust","name":"bestial Warlust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T14:36:20-08:00","id":1038583,"title":"","content":"You mean you want to convert the Dark Era to 1e, but only the fluff? Done already if that's the case. There isn't anything in there that contradicts 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T14:50:39-08:00","id":1038593,"title":"","content":"There are some creatures in the back....dragon...I believe a goblin etc.. And I was thinking how the orders would would act and how their outlook would be in due to the times (I've run a lot of Ars Magica). I was thinking about swapping out the One of the existing orders for the Order of Hermes as presented in DA:Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust","name":"bestial Warlust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T14:52:09-08:00","id":1038595,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> , the OP referenced Dark Ages: Mage, a book from Classic World of Darkness, not 1e Mage. It was about playing mages in the literal Dark Ages (ie. Medieval Europe after the collapse of the Roman Empire).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12662\" data-vbnamecard=\"12662\">bestial Warlust</a> , One of the Eras in Dark Eras is about the formation of the Orders during the time of Alexander the Great, and another is for the Neolithic period of the Vinca people, well before the orders were established.<br /> <br /> There are other eras that are Medieval Europe but not Mage specific.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T23:25:19-08:00","id":1038778,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12662\" data-vbnamecard=\"12662\">bestial Warlust</a> The only real change on the in medieval setting depends is WHEN you set the game. Before 12th century A.D. there is <b>no</b> Mysterium Order, only two of his predecessors - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993083-keepers-of-the-word-vs-pancryptiates-oh-my?p=993417#post993417\">Keepers of Word and Panscryptias</a>. Also in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034174-tremere-timeline\">8th century Tremere joined Diamond as Order</a>, but they were kicked out from alliance in 1099 A.D. onward. There is also whole<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/39919-camelot?p=41589#post41589\"> thing with Merlin in Britain</a>.<br /> <br /> If you want know more events of the <b>Mage</b> setting, I advise to look in to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/387074-history-of-awakened-mage-timeline\">History of Awakened timeline topic</a> - it's closest we have before <b>Tome of Pentacle</b> on history of Diamond. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( I still needs to add Tremere events to it, so check previously linked topic on them. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T23:34:40-08:00","id":1038780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1038525-adapting-mage-dark-ages-to-2nd-ed-mage?p=1038778#post1038778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12662\" data-vbnamecard=\"12662\">bestial Warlust</a> The only real change on the in medieval setting depends is WHEN you set the game. Before 12th century A.D. there is <b>no</b> Mysterium Order, only two of his predecessors - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993083-keepers-of-the-word-vs-pancryptiates-oh-my?p=993417#post993417\">Keepers of Word and Panscryptias</a>. Also in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034174-tremere-timeline\">8th century Tremere joined Diamond as Order</a>, but they were kicked out from alliance in 1099 A.D. onward. There is also whole<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/39919-camelot?p=41589#post41589\"> thing with Merlin in Britain</a>.<br /> <br /> If you want know more events of the <b>Mage</b> setting, I advise to look in to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/387074-history-of-awakened-mage-timeline\">History of Awakened timeline topic</a> - it's closest we have before <b>Tome of Pentacle</b> on history of Diamond. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( I still needs to add Tremere events to it, so check previously linked topic on them. )</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't the Merlin thing retroactively erased from history when the Exarchs threw a tantrum about it? In the current iteration of ChroD it didn't happen.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T03:11:11-08:00","id":1038821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1038525-adapting-mage-dark-ages-to-2nd-ed-mage?p=1038780#post1038780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't the Merlin thing retroactively erased from history when the Exarchs threw a tantrum about it? In the current iteration of ChroD it didn't happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but in Britain it seems to be the local variant of the Times Before mythology. It's an important bit of the local culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T05:49:47-08:00","id":1038846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1038525-adapting-mage-dark-ages-to-2nd-ed-mage?p=1038778#post1038778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12662\" data-vbnamecard=\"12662\">bestial Warlust</a> The only real change on the in medieval setting depends is WHEN you set the game. Before 12th century A.D. there is <b>no</b> Mysterium Order, only two of his predecessors - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993083-keepers-of-the-word-vs-pancryptiates-oh-my?p=993417#post993417\">Keepers of Word and Panscryptias</a>. Also in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034174-tremere-timeline\">8th century Tremere joined Diamond as Order</a>, but they were kicked out from alliance in 1099 A.D. onward. There is also whole<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/39919-camelot?p=41589#post41589\"> thing with Merlin in Britain</a>.<br /> <br /> If you want know more events of the <b>Mage</b> setting, I advise to look in to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/387074-history-of-awakened-mage-timeline\">History of Awakened timeline topic</a> - it's closest we have before <b>Tome of Pentacle</b> on history of Diamond. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( I still needs to add Tremere events to it, so check previously linked topic on them. )</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks I'll take a look at that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust","name":"bestial Warlust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T14:12:21-08:00","id":1039096,"title":"","content":"Here's how I'd handle the Fellowships:<br /> <br /> <b>Ahl-i-Batin</b> the Fellowship becomes Ahl-i-Batin the Legacy. Expand it a bit to make it the most popular legacy among Islamic mystics - almost a Nameless Order.<br /> <b>Messianic Voices</b> becomes a heretical offshoot of the Guardians of the Veil that identifies the Hieromagus with Christ.<br /> The <b>Old Faith</b> becomes a Nameless Order that preserves Pagan yantras and practices against persecution.<br /> The <b>Order of Hermes</b> is the Diamond Orders as they stand in this time minus the Guardians of the Veil. They have expelled the Tremere, but the Mysterium has not yet unified (based on what Wyrdhamster said above.)<br /> The <b>Spirit Talkers</b> are a loose association of mages - mainly Thyrsus, but also some Moros and Mastigos - who traffic with invisible entities and many of whom exist as solitary practitioners outside of the Diamond.<br /> The <b>Valdaermen</b> are a Nameless Order of Norse Mages who have the rare (in this time and place) ability to encode High Speech as runes for use in spellcasting.<br /> The <b>Circle of Red</b> is a loose association of antinomian Diabolists. Some traffic with Akathartoi from the Inferno, but others traffic with Abyssal entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":61,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","user":"Octavo","date":". 01-27-2017, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}